---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base>
  <section class="hero container">
    <p class="kicker">An Open-Source Agentic Gaming Studio</p>
    <h1>Fourth Wall Gaming</h1>
    <div class="divider">✦</div>
    <p class="tagline">
      AI gamemasters, worlds, art, and stories — built on the
      <strong>Mythras</strong> and <strong>Classic Fantasy</strong> ORC rules.
    </p>
    <p class="flavor">
      A table where the gamesmaster never forgets a wound, a debt, or a name.
      You speak; the world answers. The dice are honest, and the ledger is kept.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/play/">Roll Initiative</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/tech/">Read the Rules</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <div class="rules-box card">
      <p class="rules-head">How a check resolves at this table</p>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="die">d100</td><td>Roll under your skill. The difficulty grade — <em>Easy</em> to <em>Herculean</em> — is declared before the dice fall.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="die">⚔</td><td>Combat runs the full Mythras exchange: differential rolls, special effects, hit locations, armour, wounds.</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="die">✦</td><td>Every roll is returned as auditable JSON. The gamesmaster <strong>cannot</strong> fudge.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <div class="grid-3">
      <div class="card accent-ruby">
        <h3>Play It Now</h3>
        <p>Install the Mythras GM plugin for Claude Code, pick a campaign — Purewater or
        the Veilwrack — and open the first scene. Your campaign lives in a knowledge graph:
        walk away mid-scene, return weeks later, and the GM recaps exactly where you stood.</p>
        <a href="/play/">Run your first session →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card accent-amber">
        <h3>Creating Veilwrack</h3>
        <p>AI-assisted doesn't mean derivative. How the Veilwrack was made: its
        antecedents named honestly, its original ideas defended, and what worldbuilding
        at machine scale actually looks like.</p>
        <a href="/craft/">Why this isn't slop →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card accent-cobalt">
        <h3>Behind the Screen</h3>
        <p>A deterministic d100 rules engine, a TypeDB knowledge graph as the save file,
        and campaigns published as Git repos. Serious engineering in service of the
        game.</p>
        <a href="/tech/">How it works →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="divider">⚔</div>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>The Catalogue</h2>
    <div class="grid-3">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Mythras GM</h3>
        <p>A Claude-powered Gamesmaster for Mythras Imperative. Rules engine, combat
        resolution, character generation, campaign publishing — all persisted in TypeDB.</p>
        <a href="https://github.com/fourth-wall-gaming/mythras-gm">The engine, on GitHub →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>The Veilwrack: The Stilling</h3>
        <p>An original sky realm. No ground — winged peoples on the calcified husks of dead
        sky-leviathans, and the wind itself is dying. 46 lore entries, 7 factions, a
        five-act arc.</p>
        <a href="https://github.com/fourth-wall-gaming/veilwrack-campaign">The worldbook, on GitHub →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Gallery</h3>
        <p>Art, and eventually film and comics, generated alongside the worlds — every
        piece traceable to the campaign canon it illustrates.</p>
        <a href="/gallery/">Browse the gallery →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container mythras-plug">
    <div class="card accent-emerald">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0; border-bottom:none">Built on Mythras — Get the Real Game</h2>
      <p>Everything here runs on the <em>Mythras Imperative</em> SRD under the ORC License.
      Mythras is one of the finest d100 systems ever written: fast, deadly, deeply
      simulationist. If you enjoy playing it with an AI gamemaster, buy the books and
      play it with your friends.</p>
      <p>
        <a href="https://thedesignmechanism.com">The Design Mechanism</a> publishes
        <em>Mythras</em>, <em>Mythras Imperative</em>, and <em>Classic Fantasy</em>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .hero { text-align: center; padding: 3.5rem 1.25rem 1rem; }
    .kicker {
      font-variant: small-caps;
      letter-spacing: 0.22em;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      color: var(--text-dim);
      margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
    }
    .hero h1 { margin: 0.25rem 0 0; }
    .hero .divider { margin: 1.25rem auto; max-width: 18rem; }
    .tagline {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      color: var(--text);
      max-width: 38rem;
      margin: 0 auto 1rem;
    }
    .flavor {
      font-style: italic;
      color: var(--text-dim);
      max-width: 34rem;
      margin: 0 auto 2rem;
    }
    .hero-actions { display: flex; gap: 0.9rem; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    section.container { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
    .rules-box { max-width: 44rem; margin: 0 auto; }
    .rules-head {
      margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
      font-variant: small-caps;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      font-weight: 700;
      border-bottom: 2px solid var(--rule);
      padding-bottom: 0.35rem;
    }
    .rules-box table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; }
    .rules-box td { padding: 0.45rem 0.6rem 0.45rem 0; vertical-align: top; color: var(--text-dim); }
    .rules-box td.die {
      font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--ruby);
      white-space: nowrap;
      width: 3.5rem;
    }
    .mythras-plug { margin-top: 1rem; }
  </style>
</Base>
